.TH SDXI 7
.SH NAME
SDXI \- overview of the libsdxi userspace programming model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libsdxi.h>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
libsdxi is the local userspace C library for the SDXI Linux software stack.
It wraps the SDXI char-device UAPI and exposes installed public headers under
.BR sdxi/ .
.PP
The library exposes one inventory handle and two runtime handles:
.TP
.B sdxi_root_t
local device inventory object used for discovery
.TP
.B sdxi_dev_t
one opened SDXI PF or VF device node
.TP
.B sdxi_cxt_t
one local userspace context backed by a real context fd and local mappings
.PP
The installed
.BR sdxi/root.h
header exposes the local inventory API.
.SH HEADER MAP
.TP
.B sdxi/root.h
local inventory object, scan/rescan, and root-based open
.TP
.B sdxi/dev.h
device open/close, caps, attrs, OpGroup discovery
.TP
.B sdxi/dp.h
advanced local dataplane accessors and high-level helper/request structs
.TP
.B sdxi/cxt.h
context lifecycle and PASID/control-plane helpers
.TP
.B sdxi/key.h
shared RKey/AKey data model and helpers
.TP
.B sdxi/types.h
version macros, opaque handles, export annotations, common POD types
.TP
.B sdxi/util.h
generic error-formatting helpers
.TP
.B sdxi/event.h
context eventfd introspection
.TP
.B sdxi/vendor.h
generic vendor-admin transport
.TP
.B sdxi/vendor/amd_qos.h
AMD QoS admin helpers
.TP
.B sdxi/vendor/amd_crypto.h
AMD S1/S2 crypto dataplane helper types and entry points
.SH CONTROL PLANE VERSUS DATAPLANE
The public API is split into a control-plane half and a local dataplane half.
.PP
The control-plane half covers device open, capability and attribute queries,
key management, OpGroup discovery, generic vendor-admin helpers, typed AMD QoS
helpers, and context creation/destruction.
.PP
The dataplane half covers the context-owned mappings and the high-level helper
operations documented in
.BR sdxi_dp (3),
including DMA, atomic, and CRC Mode1, while typed AMD S1/S2 helpers live under
.BR sdxi_vendor_amd (3).
.PP
Raw local context-fd and mmap accessors live in
.BR sdxi_dp (3)
rather than
.BR sdxi_cxt (3)
because those details are not transport-neutral.
.SH CURRENT STATUS
The dataplane is explicitly local. A context owns mmaps and a real context fd;
it is not a transport-neutral daemon object.
.PP
Only the local backend is supported. Root creation accepts a NULL URI or
.BR sdxi:///local .
.SH RETURN VALUES
Unless a specific helper documents otherwise, libsdxi functions return 0 on
success and a negative errno-style value on failure.
.PP
Use
.BR sdxi_err_name (3)
or
.BR sdxi_err_str (3)
to format return values for diagnostics.
